Use the compiler's alloca when the C library has no <alloca.h>.

The COLR v1 glyph renderer sizes a gradient's angle table with alloca(),
which it declares by including <alloca.h> when Meson finds one (or
<malloc.h> with MSVC).  zedBSD's C library has neither the header nor a
declaration elsewhere, so the call was an implicit declaration, which C99
and the build's -Werror-implicit-function-declaration reject.  Without the
header, a GCC-compatible compiler now uses __builtin_alloca, which is what
the header would have named.  Systems with <alloca.h> are unchanged.

--- a/src/cairo-colr-glyph-render.c
+++ b/src/cairo-colr-glyph-render.c
@@ -51,6 +51,12 @@
 #include <alloca.h>
 #endif
 
+/* A C library without <alloca.h> (zedBSD) does not declare alloca at all;
+ * the compiler's builtin is what <alloca.h> would name. */
+#if !defined(HAVE_ALLOCA_H) && !defined(_MSC_VER) && !defined(alloca) && defined(__GNUC__)
+#define alloca __builtin_alloca
+#endif
+
 #if HAVE_FT_COLR_V1
 
 #include <ft2build.h>
